{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A song of ascents, of Solomon</b> — concerning Solomon, as 'and to Levi he said' [means] concerning Levi. This song one of the poets composed about Solomon, when David desired to build a house for HaShem and Nathan prophesied that Solomon his son would build it — then David rejoiced after having feared. And the poet began by stating that all is in the hand of HaShem, and not according to human designs, nor by a person's striving to strengthen his efforts with all his might. Now he began by mentioning building, which is a great need for humankind. And further, it was in David's mind to build the house, and he prepared silver, gold, and copper." "<b>in vain do its builders toil</b> — if HaShem does not help them, or if He brings a wind and destroys everything. Now he mentioned the craftsmen, who are the builders, and afterwards the guardians of the building, who are the watchmen of the city." "The word <b>שקד</b> — as in 'to watch at my doors.' And afterwards he mentioned the men of the city's commerce. And he said: <b>in vain, those who rise early</b> — for labor or for trade."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 127, :notes {0 "Resolved the elliptical comparison 'כמו וללוי אמר' by supplying 'concerning Levi' in brackets; the phrase alludes to Deuteronomy 33:8 where le- is understood as 'concerning.'", 2 "The first <b>שק</b>שקד</b> bolded as lemma head per format; the second is a quoted form. The comparison 'as in לשקוד על דלתותי' alludes to Proverbs 8:34."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:26.068106817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}